hadiths[114]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2724","narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""No woman should travel for two days except that her husband or a mahram is with her."
"2725","“It is not permissible for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to travel for more than one day’s distance without a Mahram.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2899)"
"2726","“It is not permissible for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to travel for more than one day’s distance without a Mahram.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2899)"
"2727","narrates this statement of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him: ""No woman should travel even the distance of a barid without a mahram."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) Suhail bin Abi Salih heard this hadith from his father on the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, and he also heard this narration from Sa'id Maqburi on the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him. So both of its chains are preserved."
"2728","The Messenger of Allah (SWAS) as saying : A muslim woman must not make a journey of a night unless she is accompanied by a man who is within the prohibited degrees. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1723)"
"2729","narrates this statement of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him: ""A woman should not travel except when her mahram is with her (then it is permissible)."
"2730","A woman should not set out on three (days' journey) except when she has a Mahram with her. (Using translation from Muslim 1338a)"
"2731","narrates: He heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) saying this: ""Never be alone with (a non-mahram) woman, and a woman should not travel except when she is accompanied by her mahram (close male relative)."
"2732","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is not permissible for a woman to travel except if a mahram is with her (then it is permissible)."
"2733","narrated that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade a woman from traveling unless she is accompanied by her mahram (unmarriageable kin). A woman named Umrah narrates: Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) turned her attention to some women and said, ""Is there not a mahram with each of you?"" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) did not accuse Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding this narration, because all the companions of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) are just and trustworthy. Lady Aisha's (may Allah be pleased with her) statement, ""Is there not a mahram with each of you?"" means that not every one of you has a mahram with her so that she may travel with him. Fear Allah Almighty, and none of you women should travel without a mahram."
"2734","The woman named Umrah narrates: Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) turned towards us and asked: Do none of them have a mahram with them?"
"2735","“We find (mention of) the prayer of the resident and the prayer in a state of fear in the Qur’an, but we do not find any mention of the prayer of the traveler. ‘Abdullah said to him: “Allah sent Muhammad ﷺ to us, and we did not know anything, rather we do what we saw Muhammad ﷺ doing.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1066)"
"2736","The prayer was prescribed as consisting of two rak'ahs both when one was resident and when travelling. The prayer while travelling was left according to the original prescription and the prayer of one who was resident was enhanced. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1198)"
"2737","narrates: When the prayer was made obligatory, two rak'ahs were prescribed for both residence and travel. Then, the prayer during residence was increased, and the prayer during travel was kept in its original state."
"2738","The prayers for travel and residence were made obligatory in the form of two, two rak‘ahs. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) continued to perform two, two rak‘ahs (then later the number of rak‘ahs in the prayers was increased, but) the Fajr prayer was left as it is because of its lengthy recitation. The Maghrib prayer was left as it is because it is the witr (odd-numbered prayer) of the day."
"2739","I said to 'Umar bin al Khattab ؓ , ʿAnd when you (Muslims) travel in the land, there is no sin on you if you shorten As­Salah (the prayer) if you fear that the disbelievers may put you in trial (attack you)ʿ (al Nisa' 4:101]. But now the people are safe. He said: I wondered the same thing as you are wondering, and I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about that. He said: “It is a charity that Allah has bestowed upon you, so accept His charity.ʿ (Using translation from Aḥmad 174)"
"2740","I said to ʿUmar bin al-Khattab. People are shortening the prayer today, and Allah says: “If you fear that the disbelievers may put you in trial (attack you)ʿ [an-Nisaʿ 4:101). But that time [i.e., time of fear] has gone, He said: I wondered the same thing as you are wondering, and I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about that. He said: ʿIt is a charity that Allah has bestowed upon you, so accept His charity.” ʿAbdur-Razzaq told us, Ibn Juraij told us I heard ʿAbdur-Rahman bin ‘Abdullah bin Abi ‘Ammar narrate... and he mentioned [the same report]. (Using translation from Aḥmad 244)"
"2741","Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him): People are performing shortened prayers (qasr) while Allah Almighty has stated: ""If you fear that the disbelievers may put you to trial."" But now that situation no longer exists. So Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I was also surprised at this until I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) about it, and he said: ""It is a charity which Allah Almighty has bestowed upon you, so accept His charity."
"2742","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty likes that His concession, which He has granted, be acted upon, just as He dislikes that His disobedience be committed."
"2743","I performed four rak‘ahs of the Zuhr prayer in Madinah Munawwarah behind the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and I performed two rak‘ahs of the ‘Asr prayer behind him at Dhul-Hulaifah when he was traveling."
"2744","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) performed four rak‘ahs of the Zuhr prayer in Madinah Munawwarah, and he performed two rak‘ahs of the Asr prayer at Dhul-Hulaifah. The narrator states: Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) informed us that he had heard people reciting the Talbiyah for Hajj and ‘Umrah aloud."
"2745","I asked Anas b. Malik about the shortening of the prayer (while travelling). He said: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out on a journey of three miles or three farsakh (the narrator Shu'bah doubted), he used to pray two rak'ahs. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1201)"
"2746","I performed four rak'ahs of Zuhr in Madinah Munawwarah behind the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), then he set out on a journey, and near Shajarah he led us in two rak'ahs."
"2747","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said four rak'ahs in the noon prayer while at Medina, but he offered two rak'ahs in the afternoon prayer at Dhu'l-Hulaifa. (Using translation from Muslim 690a)"
"2748","It was narrated from Anas bin Malik that the Prophet ﷺ prayed Zuhr in Al-Madinah, four Rak'ahs, and he prayed 'Asr in Dhul-Hulaifah, two Rak'ahs. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 477)"
"2749","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) stayed in Tabuk for twenty days, and during this period he continued to perform shortened prayers."
"2750","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) came to Makkah. He stayed there for seventeen days and during this period he performed shortened prayers (qasr). Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) says: Whoever stays at a place for seventeen days should perform shortened prayers, and whoever stays longer than that should perform complete prayers."
"2751","Anas bin Malik said: "" We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from Al-Madinah to Makkah and he used to lead us in praying two rak'ahs until we came back."" I (Yahya) said: ""Did he stay in Makkah?"" He (Anas) said: ""Yes, we stayed there for ten days."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1452)"
"2752","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) stayed in Tabuk for twenty (20) days and during this period he continued to perform shortened (qasr) prayers."
"2753","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) did not perform any prayer before or after (the obligatory prayer) during travel. (The narrator says:) What was meant by this is that he did not perform any (Sunnah or Nafl prayer) before or after the obligatory prayers."
"2754","""I went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from Al-Madinah to Mekkah, and he continued to shorten his prayers, and he stayed there for ten days."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1438)"
"2755","""I missed the prayer in congregation when I was in Al-Batha; how do you think I should pray?"" He said: ""Two rak'ahs, the sunnah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1444)"
"2756","I performed two rak'ahs behind the Prophet in Makkah Mukarramah on the occasion of Hajjatul Wada', even though at that time the people were many and they were in a state of greater security."
"2757","I offered prayer behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) (the narrator is in doubt), he led us in prayer at Mina, at that time we were many in number, but he led us in two rak‘ahs."
"2758","Salim b. 'Abdullah (b. 'Umar) reported on the authority of his father that Messenger of Allah ﷺ observed the prayer of a traveller, i. e. two rak'ahs in Mina, and other places; so did Abu Bakr and 'Umar, and 'Uthman too observed two rak'ahs at the beginning of his caliphate, but he then completed four. (Using translation from Muslim 694a)"
"2759","“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘When a son of Adam recites a Sajdah* and prostrates, Satan withdraws weeping, saying: ‘Woe is me! The son of Adam was commanded to prostrate and he prostrated, and Paradise will be his; I was commanded to prostrate and I refused, so I am doomed to Hell.’” * An Ayah indicating prostration. (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1052)"
"2760","narrates: Whenever the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) would recite the Qur'an and reach a verse of prostration, he would perform the prostration of recitation, and we would also perform the prostration along with him."
"2761","Abu Hurairah (led them in prayer and) recited: ""When the heaven is split asunder."" and prostrated during it. When he had finished praying, he told them that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had prostrated during it. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 961)"
"2762","""I recited to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ (Surat) An-Najm and he did not prostrate in it."" (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1404)"
"2763","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) performed the prostration of recitation in Surah An-Najm, and along with him, the Muslims, the polytheists, the jinn, and the humans also performed the prostration of recitation."
"2764","I saw that person; he was killed in a state of disbelief."
"2765","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited surah Sad on the pulpit. When he reached the place of prostration (in the surah), he descended and prostrated himself and the people prostrated with him. When the next day came, he recited it. When he reached the place of prostration (in the surah), the people became ready for prostration. Thereupon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: This is the repentance of a Prophet ; but I saw you being ready for prostration. So he descended and prostrated himself and the people prostrated along with him. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1410)"
"2766","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), ""From where did you derive the ruling of the prostration of recitation in Surah Sad?"" He recited this verse before me: ""Among his descendants are Muslims: Dawud, Sulaiman, and Ayyub."" He recited this verse up to: ""These are the ones whom Allah has guided, so follow their guidance."" Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: Sayyiduna Dawud (peace be upon him) performed prostration at this place, and for this reason, the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) also performed prostration (at this verse)."
"2767","""We prostrated with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during: When the heaven is split asunder and Read! In the Name of your Lord."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 963)"
"2768","The narrator says: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) said: I saw the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) recite a verse of prostration, and I heard him in the state of prostration reciting the same words that the man had mentioned regarding the speech of the tree."
"2769","I recited An-Najm before the Prophet, yet he did not perform a prostration. (Using translation from Bukhārī 1073)"
"2770","The sun does not rise or set on any day better than the day of Friday. Every animal remains fearful on the day of Friday except for these two groups: jinn and humans (they are not fearful)."
"2771","that He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, ""There are five actions that if done in a day, Allah will write the person from the people of Paradise: (1) visiting a sick person, (2) attending a funeral, (3) fasting for a day, (3) going to Jumuah prayer, and (5) freeing a slave."""
"2772","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that he states: I set out to visit Mount Tur and met Ka'b al-Ahbar. I sat with hi"
"2773","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is an hour on Friday during which, if any Muslim servant stands and performs prayer, and asks Allah Almighty for something during that hour, Allah Almighty grants him that thing."
"2774","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “On (the day of Jumu’ah) two angels sit at every door of the mosque who record the names of those who come first. Their example is like this: a person offered a camel as a sacrifice, then another person offered a cow as a sacrifice, then another person offered a goat as a sacrifice, then another person offered a bird as a sacrifice, then as if he gave an egg in charity. Then when the Imam sits on the pulpit, the registers are closed.”"
"2775","Whoever takes bath due to sexual defilement on Friday and goes out (for Friday prayer), is treated like one who offers a camel as sacrifice; he who goes out in the second instance as one who offers a cow; he who goes out in the third instance is treated as one who offers horned cow ; he who goes out in the fourth instance is treated as one who offers hen ; he who goes out in the fifth instance is treated as one who offers an egg. When the Imam comes out (for sermon), the angels too attend to listen to the sermon. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 351)"
"2776","narrates that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever performs ghusl on the day of Jumu'ah and purifies himself as much as possible, then applies oil or uses perfume from his house, then goes out for Jumu'ah and does not separate two people (i.e., does not push between them), then prays as much as is written for him (i.e., Sunnah or Nafl prayers), then when the Imam comes out, he remains silent (and listens to his sermon), then his sins between this Jumu'ah and the next Jumu'ah are forgiven."
"2777","“There is nothing wrong with any one of you, if he can afford it, buying two garments for Friday, other than his daily work clothes.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1096)"
"2778","narrate: We heard the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: “Whoever performs ghusl on Friday, uses the miswak, applies perfume if he has it, wears fine clothes, then goes to the mosque and does not step over people’s necks, then offers as many voluntary prayers as Allah wills, then remains silent when the imam comes until he completes the prayer, then this will be an expiation for the sins committed between this Friday and the previous Friday.”"
"2779","If anyone performs ablution, doing it well, then come to the Friday prayer, listens and keeps silence, his sins between that time and the next Friday will be forgiven, with three days extra; but he who touches pebbles has caused an interruption. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1050)"
"2780","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever performs ghusl on the day of Jumu'ah and performs ghusl well, then wears good clothes, applies perfume available in his house or applies oil, then the sins committed between that Jumu'ah and the next Jumu'ah, and in addition to that, for three more days, are forgiven."
"2781","The statement of the Prophet (peace be upon him), “Whoever gives ghusl,” means that he washes his head. And the statement, “Whoever performs ghusl,” means that he washes his body, because people used to have long hair, so they needed to wash it thoroughly. And the statement of the Prophet (peace be upon him), “He goes early and hastens,” means that he hastens for ghusl and goes early for Jumu’ah."
"2782","The statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), ""except if you are in a state of janabah,"" contains evidence that performing ghusl of janabah on the day of Jumu'ah after the break of dawn is sufficient in place of the ghusl for Jumu'ah. In this, there is evidence that performing ghusl on the day of Jumu'ah is not obligatory, because if it were obligatory, then one of the two ghusls would not suffice in place of the other."
"2783","The prayer of travel, the prayer of Eid al-Fitr, the prayer of Eid al-Adha, and the Friday prayer are two rak'ahs, and this is a complete prayer; there is no shortening in it. This matter is established from the words of your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2784","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'We are the last (to come) but will be the foremost on the Day of Resurrection, but they were given the Book before us and we were given it after them. They differed concerning this day which Allah, the Mighty and Sublime, had prescribed for them and Allah, the Mighty and Sublime, guided us to""--meaning Friday--""so the people follow us, the Jews the next day and the Christians the day after that.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1367)"
"2785","He heard Ibn Abbas and Ibn Umar narrate that while he was on the minbar, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""People should stop neglecting Jumu'ah or Allah will place a seal on their hearts and they will be deemed as being among the negligent."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1370)"
"2786","The Prophet ﷺ said: He who leaves the Friday prayer (continuously) for three Friday on account of slackness, Allah will print a stamp on his heart. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1052)"
"2787","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates this statement of the Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him: \""When a servant commits a mistake, a dot is placed upon his heart. If he separates himself from it, seeks forgiveness, and repents, then that dot is cleansed. However, if he repeats the same mistake, then it increases. If he commits the mistake again, then it increases further, until (that darkness) overcomes his heart. This is the rust which Allah, the Exalted, has me"
"2788","Sayyiduna Samurah bin Jundub (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""Whoever misses Jumu'ah should give one dinar in charity, and if he cannot afford it, then he should give half a dinar.\"""""
"2789","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Whoever misses jumu'ah with no excuse, let him give a dinar in charity, and if he cannot afford that, then half a dinar."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1372-1)"
"2790","""I was sitting beside him on Friday and he said: 'A man came, stepping over people's necks, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Sit down, you are disturbing people."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1399)"
"2791","I heard the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) say this: ""A man's prolonging of the prayer and shortening of the sermon is a sign of his understanding. So, you people should prolong the prayer and shorten the sermon, for some speech is (as effective as) magic."
"2792","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a person becomes drowsy while sitting in his place on the day of Jumu'ah, he should move to another place."
"2793","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""If you say to your companion: 'Be quiet and listen' when the imam is delivering the Khutbah, you have engaged in idle speech."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1577)"
"2794","The reason is that you spoke during the sermon of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with him) stood up and went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned this matter before him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Ubayy has spoken the truth; follow what Ubayy has said. These are the words as narrated by Abdul A’la."
"2795","When you tell (your brother on Friday) to be silent while the imam is giving the sermon you are guilty of idle talk. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1112)"
"2796","The Messenger of Allah said: ""Every Khutbah that does not have the Tashah-hud in it, then it is like a severed hand."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 1106)"
"2797","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""Every word in which there is no testimony of faith is like a severed hand.\"""""
"2798","Sayyiduna ‘Adi bin Hatim (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A man delivered a sermon in the presence of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). He said: Whoever obeys Allah and His Messenger has found guidance, and whoever disobeys both of them has gone astray. So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: This is a bad orator. You should say: Whoever disobeys Allah and His Messenger."""
"2799","I have seen you, you are ready to perform prostration, so he descended from the pulpit. He performed prostration and we also performed prostration along with him. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The correct wording is ""preparedness"" (i.e., you are prepared to do so)."
"2800","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) ordered him to come into the shade."
"2801","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would first deliver a sermon, then he would sit for a while. Then he would stand up and deliver the sermon again."
"2802","I used to pray with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and both his prayer and sermon were of moderate length. (Using translation from Muslim 866a)"
"2803","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) used to deliver a sermon on the pulpit, then he would sit down, then stand up and deliver a sermon again. He would sit between the two sermons. During the sermon, he would recite verses from the Book of Allah and admonish and advise the people."
"2804","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) stood up and said: Strive to save yourselves from Hell. Then he turned his face away and tried to protect himself. Then he said: Save yourselves from Hell. Then he turned his face away and tried to protect himself, until it seemed to us as if he was seeing it. And he said: Strive to save yourselves from Hell, even if it is with half a date. If you do not find that, then with a pure word (strive to save yourselves from Hell)."
"2805","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) descended from the pulpit after the iqamah for prayer had been pronounced. A man came and began to speak with him regarding some of his needs. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) stood with him until the man had fulfilled his need, then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) advanced and led the prayer."
"2806","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) also used to recite in the same manner."
"2807","What did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited on Friday after reciting the Surah al-Jumu'ah (62). He replied: He used to recite, ""Had the story of overwhelming event reached you ?"" (88). (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1123)"
"2808","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite in the Friday prayer: ""Glorify the name of your most high Lord"" (Surah 87) and Has the story of the overwhelming event reached you? (Surah 88). (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1125)"
"2809","""We used to pray Jumu'ah with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ then we would go back and tend to our camels."" I said: "" At what time?"" He said: ""When the sun had passed its zenith."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1390)"
"2810","We had a siesta or lunch after the Friday prayer. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1086)"
"2811","The most virtuous day in the sight of Allah Almighty is the Day of Sacrifice, and the next day after it."
"2812","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) would not leave (the house) on the day of Eid al-Fitr until he had eaten something, and on the day of sacrifice (Eid al-Adha), he would not eat anything until he had performed the sacrifice."
"2813","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) on the day of Eid al-Fitr would eat dates and then proceed (towards the Eid prayer ground)."
"2814","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) would not go out on the day of Eid al-Fitr until he had eaten three, or five, or seven dates."
"2815","narrates: When the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) would go out for the two Eids, he would return by a different route than the one by which he had gone."
"2816","“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to bring them (the women) out on the day of Fitr and the day of Nahr.” Umm ‘Atiyyah said: “We said: ‘What if one of them does not have an outer covering?’ He said: ‘Let her sister share her own outer covering with her.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1307)"
"2817","""Messenger of Allah would order the virgins, the mature women, the secluded and the menstruating to go out for the two Eid. As for the menstruating women, they were to stay away from the Musalla and participate in the Muslims supplications."" One of them said: 'O Messenger of Allah! What if she does not have a Jilbab? He said: 'Then let her sis lend her a Jilbab.'"" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 539)"
"2818","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) went out on the day of Eid al-Fitr, or perhaps Eid al-Adha, and he led the people in two rak‘ahs. Then, after completing the prayer, he did not perform any (optional prayer) before or after it."
"2819","I prayed the 'Id prayer with the Prophet ﷺ not once or twice (but many times) without the adhan and the iqamah. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1148)"
"2820","""Umar bin Al-Khattab asked Abu Waqid Al-Laithi what Messenger of Allah would recite during Al-Fitr and Al-Adha, so he said: 'He would recite: Qaf, By the Glorious Quran and the Hour has drawn near, and the moon has been cleft asunder.'"" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 534)"
"2821","It was narrated from Nu’man bin Bashir that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite “Glorify the Name of your Lord, the Most High,” [Al-A’la (87)] and “Has there come to you the narration of the overwhelming?” [Al-Ghashiyah (88)] in the ‘Eid prayer. (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1281)"
"2822","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite 'Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High'(Al-A'la 87) and 'Has there come to you the narration of the overwhelming (i.e. the Day of Resurrection)?' (Al-Ghashiyah 88) in the Jumu'ah prayer, and sometimes 'Eid and Jumu'ah would fall on the same day, and he would recite them in both 'Eid and Jumu'ah prayer."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1424)"
"2823","Ibn ʿAbbas was asked whether he had joined the Prophet ﷺ in the ʿId prayer. He said, ""Yes. And I could not have joined him had I not been young. (The Prophet ﷺ came out) till he reached the mark which was near the house of Kathir bin As-Salt, offered the prayer, delivered the Khutba and then went towards the women. Bilal was accompanying him. He preached to them and advised them and ordered them to give alms. I saw the women putting their ornaments with their outstretched hands into Bilal's garment. Then the Prophet ﷺ along with Bilal returned home. (Using translation from Bukhārī 977)"
"2824","I bear witness regarding the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) that he went out with his companions on the day of Eid al-Fitr. He performed the prayer, then delivered the sermon, then he went to the women and instructed them to give charity, so they began to give charity."
"2825","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) delivered the sermon on the day of Eid standing on his feet (i.e., on the ground)."
"2826","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) used to first perform the Eid al-Fitr and Eid al-Adha prayers, then deliver the sermon."
"2827","narrates: During the blessed time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), there was a solar eclipse. This happened on the day when (the son of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) Sayyiduna Ibrahim (may Allah be pleased with him) passed away. People said: This eclipse has occurred because of the death of Sayyiduna Ibrahim (may Allah be pleased with him). So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed, the sun and the moon are two signs among the signs of Allah. They do not eclipse because of anyone’s death or life. When you see them (in the state of eclipse), supplicate and perform prayer until they become clear."
"2828","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""The sun and moon do not become eclipsed for death or birth of anyone, rather they are two of the signs of Allah (SWT) the Most High, so when you see that then pray."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1461)"
"2829","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) stood up and we stood up following him. Then he said: ""O people! Indeed, the sun and the moon are two signs among the signs of Allah. If either of them is eclipsed, then come to the mosques (that is, perform the eclipse prayer)."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) In this narration, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) has commanded to perform prayer at the time of a solar or lunar eclipse, and this is the intended purpose. So here, the purpose has been mentioned in absolute terms with its cause, and that is the mosques, because prayer is performed in the mosque. It is not that merely coming to the mosque at the time of a solar or lunar eclipse will suffice if the prayer is not performed."
"2830","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) on the authority of Abdul Malik bin Abu Sulaiman from Ata."
"2831","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed on the day the sun was eclipsed, bowing four times in two rak'ahs and prostrating four times. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1469)"
"2832","""There was an eclipse of the sun and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed and the people with him. He stood for long time reciting something like Surah Al-Baqarah, then he raised (his head) and stood for a long time, then he raised (his head) and stood for a long time which was shorter than the first time. Then he bowed for a long time, which was shorter than the first time, then he prostrated. Then he got up and stood for a long time, which was shorter than the first time, then he bowed for a long time, which was shorter than the first time, then he raised (his head) and stood for a long time, which was shorter than the first time. Then he bowed for a long time, which was shorter than the first time, then he prostrated, then he finished (his prayer) and the sun had been clear. He said: 'The sun and the moon are two of the signs of Allah (SWT) and they do not become eclipsed for the death or birth of anyone. If you see that then remember Allah (SWT) the Mighty and Sublime.' They said: 'O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, we saw you stretching out your hand when you were standing, then we saw you moving backward. He said: 'I saw Paradise-or it was shown to me- and I reached out to a take a bunch of its fruits. If I ha taken it you would have eaten from it for as long as this world lasts. And I saw Hell and I have never seen anything like it, and I saw that most of its inhabitants are women.' They said: ""Why, O Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said: 'Because of their ingratitude.' It was said: 'Are they ungrateful to Allah?' He said: 'They are ungrateful to their husbands and they are ungrateful for kind treatment. If you are kind to one of them for a lifetime, then she sees (one) bad thing from you, she will say: I have never seen anything good from you.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1493)"
"2833","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the sun and the moon do not eclipse because of anyone's death or life. When you see either of them (in the state of eclipse), perform prayer until it becomes bright again or Allah makes a new decision."
"2834","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) stood up in anxiety, dragging his cloak, and entered the mosque. He performed two units of prayer. While he was still praying, the eclipse ended. This eclipse occurred at the time of the death of the Prophet’s (peace and blessings be upon him) son, Sayyiduna Ibrahim (may Allah be pleased with him), so some people said: The eclipse happened because of Ibrahim’s death. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “O people! Indeed, the sun and the moon are two signs among the signs of Allah. They do not eclipse because of anyone’s death. When you see them (in the state of eclipse), supplicate until the eclipse is over.” (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), “Supplicate,” means that you should perform prayer, because sometimes the Arabs use the word supplication for prayer."
"2835","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) hurriedly went inside the mosque, dragging his lower garment (the narrator is unsure, perhaps these are the words: he was dragging his garment). People also gathered around him. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) led them in two units of prayer, just as you perform prayer. The eclipse ended. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) turned towards the people, and they gathered around him. He said: Indeed, the sun and the moon are two signs among the signs of Allah, by which Allah causes fear in His servants. These two do not eclipse because of anyone’s death. (The narrator says) The son of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) had passed away. (The Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, said) When you see any of these things (i.e., when you see an eclipse), then keep performing prayer until the eclipse ends. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The statement of Sayyiduna Abu Bakrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) led them in two units of prayer, just as you perform prayer, means: just as you perform two units of prayer for the eclipse, in which there are four bowings (ruku) and four prostrations (sujood), as we have mentioned earlier."
"2836","""There was an eclipse of the sun, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ got up in a rush, fearing that it might be the Hour. He went to the masjid, where he stood and prayed, standing, bowing and prostrating for the longest time that I ever saw him do in prayer. Then he said: 'These signs that Allah (SWT) sends do not occur for the death or birth of anyone, but Allah (SWT) sends them to strike fear into His slaves. If you see any of these things, then hasten to remember Him, call upon Him supplicate and ask for His forgiveness.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1503)"
"2837","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) performed two rak‘ahs in the prayer of the solar and lunar eclipse, which were like your prayer. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) Sayyiduna Abu Bakrah’s (may Allah be pleased with him) statement that “two rak‘ahs like your prayer” means, as you people perform the eclipse prayer."
